# .dockerignore — keep the build context to the Go module sources (w6-02).
#
# Everything listed below never leaves the host: it cannot reach the daemon,
# the layer cache, or an image layer. That is the structural guarantee behind
# "no test fixtures, no VCS history, no tokens in the image" (w6-02
# acceptance) — the Dockerfile COPYs only cmd/ internal/ rules/ adapters/,
# and this file makes sure the context itself carries nothing else.
#
# Kept in the context: go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/, rules/, adapters/,
# Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, .dockerignore.

# Version-control and CI metadata (never ship history or workflow files).
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github

# Local factory scaffolding (worktrees, reference clones — gitignored too).
.worktrees
.reference
reference

# Test fixtures and corpora: large, and never needed at runtime. Scanning a
# repo is the user's job at runtime (`-v "$PWD:/src:ro"`), not the image's.
testdata

# Documentation, reports and tooling — not part of the binary.
docs
reports
tools
Makefile
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
*.md

# Release/build artifacts and local state.
dist
bin
.goreleaser.yaml
.vanguard.example.yaml
.editorconfig
node_modules
*.log
